+{
+  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
+  "demand_id": "BADF-DEM-0118",
+  "kind": "issue",
+  "source": {
+    "repository": "bstBizEra/badf",
+    "issue": 277,
+    "url": "https://github.com/bstBizEra/badf/issues/277",
+    "exported_at": "2026-09-01T08:00:00Z",
+    "body_digest": "sha256:0c5017b55419508c9ffb3dca401377eb3a46ba8387a9efb1594c9133beb9c7ba"
+  },
+  "title": "UAT-D (shadow): badf-uat has an EMPTY corpus — BADF has never run a G10, so 'shadow' must be declared-empty or the rung is blocked",
+  "problem": "🧠 **ARCHI (BARCHI-3)** — rung **D** of `badf-uat`'s A→E ladder. **Posting the plan and stopping, because the measured corpus is empty and that changes what D can honestly be.**\n\n## The measurement that reframes this rung\n\nThe `badf-build` shadow doctrine (`BLD-D`, #197) is the pattern D would normally follow: a record generated once from history and **recomputed on every run** against the object store, so it cannot drift; a tampered record refused; a control with no historical corpus **declared** non-coverage, never implied.\n\nThat pattern needs history. Measured on `origin/main` at `bc7ca27`:\n\n```\nG10 dossiers ever assembled                     0\nlanded evidence with evidence_type \"uat\"        0   (only hits are this family's own test file)\ngate-dossier.G07 on main                       91\n```\n\n**BADF has never run a G10.** It builds itself; it has no product-acceptance event. So there is no corpus, and the `build` pattern is unavailable — not deferred, unavailable.\n\n## Why the obvious workaround is refused up front\n\nThe tempting move is to shadow `uat` over the 91 G07 dossiers, or to synthesize a corpus and call the result a shadow. **Both are the proxy-for-property class** — `badf-build`'s shadow means something *because* the corpus is real landed evidence produced by the real workflow. A synthetic corpus measures the fixture, and a G07 corpus measures a different gate. A shadow rung that shadows nothing would report exactly as green as one that shadowed everything, which is the defect this ladder has spent five rungs closing.\n\n## Proposed shape — D is a declared-empty shadow, and says so\n\n1. `examples/uat-shadow-evidence.json` with `corpus: []`, `counts` all zero, and `non_coverage` carrying **one entry per control** (U2–U5, C7–C11) stating *no landed G10 evidence exists to replay it against* — the `build` doctrine's \"declared, never implied\" applied to a corpus that is empty rather than partial.\n2. `skills/badf-uat/evidence/shadow-evidence.md` stating the emptiness, **what would constitute a corpus** (the first real G10 dossier), and the re-measurement trigger.\n3. `tests/test_badf_uat_shadow.py` asserting: the record is recomputed not stored; `corpus == []` is **asserted against the live tree**, so the day a real G10 dossier lands this test goes RED and forces the rung to be redone — an emptiness claim that expires by itself rather than by anyone remembering.\n4. **No registry status change.** `badf-uat` stays `IMPLEMENTED`.\n\n## The load-bearing question for review — I am not deciding it alone\n\n**Does an empty-corpus shadow satisfy D, or is D genuinely blocked until BADF has a product to accept?**\n\n- If it satisfies D: the ladder proceeds, E (admission) follows, and `badf-uat` reaches `ACTIVE` **never having been exercised against a real acceptance** — a family that is law without ever having been observed working.\n- If it does not: `badf-uat` stops at `IMPLEMENTED` until a real G10 exists, and the A→E ladder is documented as **not completable** for a product gate inside a self-building framework.\n\nI lean to the second being the honest answer and the first being the useful one, which is precisely why it is not mine to settle quietly. **`badf-release-validation` (G09) sits at `IMPLEMENTED` and may face the same wall at its own D** — so the answer is a precedent for every product-side gate, not just this family.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (if shape 1–4 is approved)\n\n- `corpus == []` asserted against a live scan of `work/*/gate-dossier.G10.json` — red the moment one exists.\n- One `non_coverage` entry per named control, each naming the control and the reason; test asserts the set of entries **equals** the set of controls, so a control added later without a shadow entry fails.\n- Tampering with the stored record is refused (recomputation, not trust).\n- `test_no_registry_status_change_at_d` — D does not advance the ladder.\n- Scope: no adapter, no `lifecycle.json` change, no second gate (UAT-I20), no `badf-production-readiness` surface.\n\n**Version tier:** patch (evidence + docs + tests; no behaviour change).\n**Stage-gate:** DEV Glossary stage 11 (validation), maturity 4.\n**Lean mode:** advisory.\n\n<!-- agent: architect -->\n\n",
+  "authorized_by": {
+    "principal": "operator",
+    "principal_type": "human"
+  },
+  "recorded_at": "2026-09-01T08:00:00Z",
+  "provenance": {
+    "agent": "BARCHI-3",
+    "seat": "architect",
+    "note": "SARCHI ruled on #277 and amended the ruling within the hour; the amended disposition (representative shadow + declared caveat + mechanical tripwire) is what this demand carries."
+  },
+  "status": "AUTHORIZED"
+}
